From: Pivox build system
Subject: [PATCH] absl/time: use CMake 3.24 $<LINK_LIBRARY:FRAMEWORK> form

Upstream already has a TODO (#1495) to switch from the clang-driver-specific
"-Wl,-framework,CoreFoundation" shorthand to the neutral
$<LINK_LIBRARY:FRAMEWORK,CoreFoundation> generator expression once their
minimum CMake version reaches 3.24. Pivox requires CMake 4.0, so we apply
that fix early. Without it, swiftc (which doesn't parse -Wl,X,Y,Z) fails
to link any Swift target that transitively consumes absl::time via gRPC.

--- a/absl/time/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/absl/time/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -81,9 +81,7 @@ absl_cc_library(
     ${ABSL_DEFAULT_COPTS}
   DEPS
     Threads::Threads
-    # TODO(#1495): Use $<LINK_LIBRARY:FRAMEWORK,CoreFoundation> once our
-    # minimum CMake version >= 3.24
-    $<$<PLATFORM_ID:Darwin,iOS,tvOS,visionOS,watchOS>:-Wl,-framework,CoreFoundation>
+    $<$<PLATFORM_ID:Darwin,iOS,tvOS,visionOS,watchOS>:$<LINK_LIBRARY:FRAMEWORK,CoreFoundation>>
 )

 # Internal-only target, do not depend on directly.
